UDFBench Q1-derived data preparation

This independently authored preparation script uses Apache-2.0. It downloads
unmodified originals outside the Sirius source tree for an executable oracle.
Downloaded UDFBench source files retain their GPL-3.0 license, reproduced in
the external output directory as sources/LICENSE; they are not Sirius source.

Original benchmark: Yannis Foufoulas, Theoni Palaiologou, and Alkis Simitsis.
The UDFBench Benchmark for General-purpose UDF Queries. PVLDB 18(9), 2025.
doi:10.14778/3746405.3746409.
Repository: https://github.com/athenarc/UDFBench
Pinned commit: 8da987566590e2534f24cd97bcfaa9157c24962c

The public tiny artifacts CSV is downloaded from that pinned repository.
Its associated dataset record declares Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International (CC-BY-4.0): https://zenodo.org/records/14260428
License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Repository and dataset-record licenses are recorded separately in the generated
provenance.json. Fields are projected and expected values are generated by the
original Python functions, checked against an independent restricted reference.
Scaling repeats public rows and does not represent an official dataset scale.

The adaptation supports NULL, empty, or exactly ASCII YYYY-MM-DD-shaped strings,
without calendar validation. Out-of-domain strings produce NULL; equivalence to
the original functions outside that domain is not claimed. Preparation refuses
out-of-domain dates in the source dataset. No complete UDFBench-suite reproduction
or confidential customer data or logic is included.
